  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California received $43.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 191,418 awards, with an average award size of $228K, and obligations fell 29.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations peaked in FY25 at $62B, then decreased to $43.7B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in California, obligating $23.3B so far in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Energy with $6.3B and the Department of Homeland Security with $4.8B. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the top vendor at $3.4B, with FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO at $2.5B and NATIONAL STEEL AND SHIPBUILDING COMPANY at $1.9B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations at $5.9B, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.3B and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $4B. All figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date.",
