        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations are $43.7B compared with $62B in FY25 and $61.7B in FY24. Obligations fell 29.5% year over year. The state recorded 191,418 awards in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $228K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which federal agencies and vendors dominate California contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $23.3B in FY2026 to date, more than any other agency. The Department of Energy obligated $6.3B and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $4.8B. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC received $3.4B, FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO received $2.5B, and NATIONAL STEEL AND SHIPBUILDING COMPANY received $1.9B."
      }
